Engine activity narrator: reformats --enable-logging-iteration-details'
per-step log line to name the actual requests instead of just counts, and
replaces its elapsed_ms field (unreliable under --async-scheduling, see
_log_iteration_details()'s docstring below) with a real wall-clock rate
computed from the gap between log calls. See REQUEST_LOGGING_SPEC.md Part
5. No new CLI flag: reuses vLLM's existing --enable-logging-iteration-details
toggle, wired to this repo's ITERATION_LOG env var in start_qwen.sh.

Before:
  Engine 000: Iteration(42): 3 context requests, 6144 context tokens, 0
  generation requests, 0 generation tokens, iteration elapsed time: 0.05
  ms, GPU KV cache usage: 41.2%

After:
  Engine 000: prompt processing [chatcmpl-a1b2, chatcmpl-c3d4, chatcmpl-e5f6]
  (3 reqs, 6144 tokens) = 3792.3 tok/s | GPU KV cache usage: 41.2%

Four files, all data already computed and just not threaded through
before: SchedulerIterationDetails/IterationDetails gain per-request id +
token-count lists (v1/metrics/stats.py, v1/utils.py) populated in
compute_iteration_details()'s existing per-request loop (v1/utils.py) and
copied through in capture_iteration_details() (v1/engine/core.py); the
reformatting and corrected timing live entirely in
LoggingStatLogger._log_iteration_details() (v1/metrics/loggers.py) — no
change to the cross-process wire format's compatibility (verified the new
list[str]/list[int] fields round-trip through msgspec.msgpack encode/decode
of EngineCoreOutputs, the actual struct these stats travel inside from the
EngineCore process to the API server process).

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/iteration-details-reqids.patch

